          DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW VERSION OF DEC/EDI SOFTWARE


LONDON -- October 31, 1995 --- Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced Version 3.0 of its DEC/EDI software, a significantly 
enhanced version of the industry's first client/server, enterprise-
wide software for Electronic Data Interchange (EDI).

     DEC/EDI Version 3.0 software provides users with the capability 
to take full advantage of DEC/EDI's client/server architecture while 
running the server components in a UNIX environment.

     The DEC/EDI Version 3.0 software also introduces the DEC/EDI 
CommandCenter which provides EDI administrators with an extensive 
set of configuration and monitoring functions for entering and 
managing EDI information from a graphical user interface (GUI) 
running under Microsoft Windows.

     DEC/EDI software provides the foundation for enterprise-wide 
electronic commerce. It integrates a wide range of trading partner 
communications services, including X.435, X.400, OFTP and 
Bisynchronous. It also integrates EDI translation services for ANSI 
X12, UN/EDIFACT, TRADACOMS, and industry specific transactions, as 
well as application integration tools and electronic mail and 
workflow to deliver comprehensive electronic commerce solutions.

     Wayne Toye, Digital's EDI Marketing Manager, said the DEC/EDI 
Version 3.0 enhancements "demonstrate Digital's continuing 
commitment to maintain leadership software in enterprise-wide EDI 
and electronic commerce for today's multi-platform business 
applications and operating environments.

     "We've made it easier for businesses to exchange EDI 
transaction data with trading partners by extending our mixed 
platform and mixed network environments to support EDI server 
software for both the OpenVMS and Digital UNIX operating systems," 
Toye noted.

     Digital's DEC/EDI software now supports Alpha and VAX platforms 
running under OpenVMS, as well as Alpha platforms running under 
Digital UNIX. 

     DEC/EDI also continues to support a wide range of business 
applications through application clients that run in OpenVMS (Alpha 
and VAX), Digital UNIX (Alpha), HP-UX, IBM AIX, and MVS-CICS, 
MVS-Batch and VSE-CICS operating environments.

     The new DEC/EDI CommandCenter makes it easy to create and 
maintain DEC/EDI system information, EDI messages and transactions, 
trading partner profiles, mapping tables, and communications 
options.

     The DEC/EDI CommandCenter, through a graphical user interface 
(GUI), provides features such as cut/copy/paste, drop down lists 
where selections are made from a pre-defined set of options, and 
extensive defaults that enable users to enter and manage EDI 
information.

     Nad Nadesan, Digital's EDI Product Manager, said the easy-to-
use DEC/EDI CommandCenter can "maintain more than one DEC/EDI server 
and can transfer configuration information between servers.

     "It even can carry out CommandCenter functions when it is not 
connected to the DEC/EDI server," Nadesan added.

The DEC/EDI CommandCenter provides the capability to:

     o 	register remote and local application clients and the 
        business applications which will use each application 
        client.

     o 	edit existing EDI messages/transactions to conform to 
        trading partner agreements, and create new EDI messages/
     	transactions.

     o 	identify trading partners who can send or receive data, 
        which EDI documents are to be exchanged, and the 
        communications links and addressing information to be used.

     o 	define how the format of data sent or received by the 
        business application maps to the format of data for EDI 
        messages/transactions.

     o 	define which communications options are being used, and the 
        parameters of individual communications links.

     o 	and, perform the functions of the EDI Cockpit by providing 
        simplified access to the status of EDI transactions.

     DEC/EDI Version 3.0 is available immediately worldwide, and 
pricing ranges from $9,000 to $20,000 depending on system size and 
user licensing. Pricing for the DEC/EDI CommandCenter is $2,500.

     Digital provides complete solutions for implementing EDI and 
electronic commerce and systems integration capabilities to 
integrating these solutions into business processes.

     Digital has been providing DEC/EDI software since 1990, when it 
introduced the industry's first client/server EDI software. There 
are currently more than 600 DEC/EDI implementations in more than 40 
countries worldwide. 

     Built on decades of experience in networking, electronic 
messaging and Digital's own EDI implementation, DEC/EDI and its 
integration with the MAILbus family of electronic messaging products 
enables users to grow easily from basic EDI into an enterprise-wide 
Electronic Commerce implementation.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systema. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
