            NEW MESSAGING SOFTWARE FROM DIGITAL CONNECTS
            INTERNET, X.400, and IBM SNADS ENVIRONMENTS;
                  PROVIDES DESKTOP X.500 MANAGEMENT


MAYNARD, Mass., November 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation, 
one of the world's leading suppliers of global messaging solutions, 
today announced software that makes it easier for companies to 
exchange and manage information across heterogeneous electronic mail 
systems.  

     Two new products will improve connectivity among X.400, 
Internet, and IBM SNADS messaging environments. A new information 
manager will enable easier management of X.500 directory information 
from the administrator's desktop.

Announced today are the following connectivity software products:

     o 	The MAILbus 400 SMTP Gateway V2.0 for Digital UNIX -- 
        includes new functionality enabling Multipurpose Internet 
        Mail Extensions (MIME) with 8-bit support for the transfer 
        of text, complex documents and binary files between Internet 
        and X.400 mail systems.

     o 	The SNADS Gateway for Digital Mailbus 400 V1.0 -- a third 
        party offering from X.gate Limited of the United Kingdom 
        that provides connectivity between an X.400 environment and 
        IBM SNADS mail systems such as OfficeVision/MVS, 
        OfficeVision/400, and Verimation's Memo.

     o 	The Digital X.500 Information Manager V1.0 for Windows -- 
        that provides an easy to use graphical interface on Windows 
        95 and Windows NT Intel-based desktops for managing all 
        MAILbus 400 routing information across geographically 
        dispersed systems.

     "As more corporations seek to link diverse messaging systems 
together and enable message exchange through the Internet, the need 
for reliable, flexible and manageable messaging software is growing 
dramatically," said Gerard van de Aast, vice president of Digital's 
Enterprise Software Group.  "The software solutions that we are 
announcing today represent some of the initial offerings from 
Digital's new Connectivity Software Business Unit, and are designed 
to provide customers with seamless messaging services across 
heterogeneous mail environments."

     X.400 is the messaging protocol of choice among many large 
organizations seeking secure, robust global messaging.  With more 
than 3000 companies worldwide using MAILbus products, Digital is the 
leading provider of X.400 compliant messaging backbone software.  As 
these users increasingly access the Internet, they have been 
requesting ways to exchange spreadsheets, formatted word processing 
documents and other complex documents seamlessly. 

     The MAILbus SMTP Gateway V2.0 software announced today, 
features support for the Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions 
(MIME) which provide users with this seamless communication 
capability.  Both of these new products are integrated with the 
MAILbus 400 management services and give administrators a seamless 
view of their heterogeneous messaging environment.

     "Digital has taken another step forward in integrating the 
world's most popular global messaging systems," says Hans Ole S. 
Andersen, System Manager at Tele Danmark, a leading provider of 
telecommunication services. "The inclusion of MIME support in the 
SMTP Gateway has enabled Tele Danmark to seamlessly transfer 
attachments, complex documents and binary files between the Internet 
and X.400 mail systems.  The users of these systems expect the 
transfer of messages to be effortless, and these new products from 
Digital enable us to accomplish that."

     The SNADS Gateway for Digital MAILbus 400 connects users of 
Digital's messaging products to popular IBM messaging environments.  
Available from X.gate Limited, this electronic mail gateway provides 
a closely coupled connection between Digital's MAILbus 400 systems 
and mail systems based on IBM SNADS.  This product exchanges text 
notes, FFT, RFT and binary files. As a full-featured agent it is 
designed to provide throughput of up to 2000 text items per hour.  
In addition, robust remote network management support utilizing 
POLYCENTER Manager on Netview is provided.  

     The X.500 Information Manager provides an easy to use interface 
that enables administrators to browse, modify and create X.500 
directory entries from Microsoft Windows 95 and Windows NT 
environments.  The Information Manager has a graphical user 
interface that enables an administrator to manage users' mail 
addresses and messaging system information across heterogeneous mail 
systems, thereby eliminating the need to enter the same data more 
than once.

     According to Richard Thibodeau, Director of Multimedia 
Messaging for WorldLinx Telecommunications, "We recognized our need 
for next generation technology, not only in terms of enhanced 
messaging services, but also X.500 directory services. We were 
looking for a vendor who could supply both. In addition, we wanted to 
work with a company that had a clear messaging vision that matched our 
own.  Digital was unique in its ability to provide all of these.  They 
demonstrated a commitment, and a desire to do business that was second 
to none."  WorldLinx is a Toronto-based subsidiary of Bell Canada and 
provides business communications services.

     Digital is committed to providing seamless messaging 
capabilities across the enterprise.  Microsoft has joined Digital in 
delivering complementary products to address enterprise requirements 
for electronic mail solutions.  This will enable the five million 
users of ALL-IN-1 and MailWorks to easily use or access Microsoft 
Exchange functionality, and Digital's MAILbus 400 products will give 
Microsoft Exchange users access to other mail environments as 
illustrated by the products announced today.

Pricing and Availability

     The MAILbus 400 SMTP Gateway V2.0 for Digital UNIX license has 
a list price of $7,889.00 and the documentation kit is available for 
$564.00  The Digital X.500 Information Manager V1.0 for Windows is 
priced at $600.00 for a single user license.  The SNADS Gateway for 
Digital MAILbus 400 V1.0 has a list price of $20,000.  All of these 
products are currently shipping. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
