                 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES INTENT TO DEVELOP
            PENTIUM PRO PROCESSOR SMP ENTERPRISE SERVERS 


     Demonstrates 200MHz Pentium Pro Superserver at Intel Event


MAYNARD, Mass., November 7, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it will extend its family of award-winning 
Prioris servers with a superserver based on Intel's recently 
announced PentiumbPro processor.  The Pentium Pro processor server 
will feature Digital-engineered main logic boards to enable the 
highest level of performance and reliability for enterprise-class
client/server computing.  At an Intel Corporation press conference 
in New York City today, Digital demonstrated a four processor 
symmetrical multiprocessing (SMP) superserver based on 200MHz Intel 
Pentium Pro microprocessors. The Prioris Pentium Pro superserver is 
scheduled to ship in the first quarter of 1996.

     "With the Pentium Pro processor, performance is no longer an 
issue for Intel-based servers in the enterprise," said Duane 
Dickhut, vice president of Digital's PC Server Product Line. 
"Coupled with our leadership work in Windows NT clusters, our new 
system and network management software tools, and our corporate 
legacy of excellence in networked computing, Digital is uniquely
positioned to take a leadership role in the enterprise-class, 
Intel-based superserver market."

     The Digital/Microsoft Alliance for Enterprise Computing, 
combines Microsoft client/server products with Digital's leadership 
in enterprise systems, service, support and systems integration, and 
enables customers to deploy business solutions on the Microsoft 
Windows and Windows NT operating systems with assurance of 
integration into the most complex business environments.  In
addition, Digital's close relationships with independent software 
vendors in the connectivity and database realms, further bolster the 
company's standing as the vendor of choice in client/server 
enterprise computing.

     As with all Digital Prioris PC servers, the new Pentium Pro 
processor enterprise-class machine is slated to include -- at no 
extra cost -- Digital's recently announced ServerWORKS Manager 
system and network management software and ServerWORKS Quick Launch, 
a CD-ROM suite of utilities that automates network operating system 
installation and the configuration of Digital Prioris PC servers.

     The upcoming Prioris Pentium Pro processor-based machine will 
be targeted at the most performance-intensive applications in 
client/server computing, including large database tasks, multimedia 
and high-traffic Internet communications.  The Prioris with Pentium 
Pro processors will be scalable from one-to-four CPUs in an SMP 
configuration. To ensure maximum availability and performance for 
mission-critical tasks, the Pentium Pro system will feature ECC
memory, hot-swappable disk drives, redundant power and cooling, 
Fast/Wide SCSI, multichannel RAID and high-bandwidth PCI I/O.  The 
Pentium Pro-based systems will continue to deliver on the Digital 
PC server value proposition of industry-leading performance, 
expandability and scalability to provide maximum investment 
protection.  

     Digital has been working closely with Intel as a Validation 
Partner for the Pentium Pro processor.  Digital was selected by 
Intel as a Validation Partner as a result of the superior 
performance and engineering excellence of its current family of 
Prioris servers.  Digital's Prioris Intel-based servers effectively 
span the range of server applications by balancing power and price
to match a wide range of business needs.  The entire line of Prioris 
PC servers incorporates balanced system design and robust fault-
tolerance for maximum server performance while maintaining 
aggressive PC price points.

     When it is commercially available, the new Prioris superserver 
will support a wide range of operating environments, including 
Windows NT Server 3.51; Novell NetWare 3.X, 4.X and NetWare SMP; SCO 
UnixWare; SCO Open Server 5.0; IBM OS/2 SMP; Banyan VINES; and 
Digital PATHWORKS.

     The system will be covered by a standard three-year, on-site 
limited warranty, with next-business day response standard from 
Digital's Multivendor Customer Services organization or an 
authorized Digital Warranty Service Provider.

     The Prioris Pentium Pro processor-based superserver is planned 
for availability in the first quarter of 1996 through Digital's 
channel partners, including master resellers, wholesalers, 
distributors, dealers, VARs and system integrators.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
