        LOTUS AND DIGITAL ANNOUNCE PLANS FOR NOTES SOLUTIONS
                     ON DIGITAL ALPHA PLATFORMS


     Relationship Includes Development of the first 64-bit Notes
                           Implementation


CAMBRIDGE, Mass., November 6, 1995 -- Lotus Development Corporation 
and Digital Equipment Corporation today announced a multi-faceted 
agreement under which Lotus will provide Lotus Notes integrated 
groupware and messaging products to Digital customers on Digital 
Alpha-based systems.

The companies announced that Digitals worldwide sales force will 
continue to sell Lotus Notes through its Multivendor Customer 
Services' existing reseller agreement with Lotus.  Digitals 
Multivendor Customer Services organization offers installation and 
technical support, as well as Help Desk support for customers who 
have multi-platform environments which include Lotus Notes.  Lotus 
will develop versions of Lotus Notes Release 4 for both the Digital 
UNIX and Windows NT operating systems for Digitals Alpha processor.  
Lotus expects to deliver the Alpha versions of Notes for Windows NT 
during the first half of 1996.  Lotus expects to deliver the Alpha 
versions of Notes for Digital UNIX during the second half of 1996.

Digital has had a business partner relationship with Lotus for over 
10 years and has been a Lotus Passport reseller since 1994.  In 
response to its business and distribution channel partner requests, 
Digital has been using Notes for an information exchange medium in 
business process re-engineering projects.  

"The agreement with Digital is a further expression of Lotus 
commitment to provide truly open multi-platform groupware 
solutions," said Jeff Papows, Lotus Executive Vice President and 
Chief Operating Officer.  "Lotus Notes is the industry leading 
groupware and messaging product.  Independent studies are now 
confirming what we have learned through six years of in-market 
experience with Notes -- that the return on investment in groupware 
increases exponentially when it is used to extend enterprise 
communications to include customers, suppliers and business 
partners.  Notes is the only multi-platform groupware solution to 
greatly facilitate this.  The addition of these highly valued 
Digital platforms is another significant indication of our continued 
commitment to making Notes the cross-platform standard for 
organizations worldwide looking to enhance communication, 
collaboration and coordination within and beyond their 
organizations."

Enrico Pesatori, Digitals Vice President and General Manager, 
Computer Systems Division said, Notes availability on Alpha 
platforms is extremely important.  With Digitals integrated 
Intel/Alpha platform strategy, customers can start today on a 
Digital Intel solution and move forward with assurance that 
Alpha-based solutions will be available in the future.  Customers 
will now be able to choose one of todays most widely accepted 
multi-platform enterprise solutions and plan to deploy it on the 
industries best performing RISC platforms from Digital.  Many 
organizations will now be able to move forward to re-engineer 
business processes with Notes without the distraction of concerns 
about scalability, manageability, or interoperability.  Digitals 
long history in meeting the needs of Enterprises, coupled with Notes 
high ROI and platform flexibility, make this a big win for our 
customers.  For our UNIX customers, the worlds first 64-bit version 
of Lotus Notes will be our recommended solution."

Lotus Notes will be made available on the full line of Digitals 
Alpha processors.  Digitals 64-bit AlphaServer line comprises 
systems ranging from the mainframe class AlphaServer 8400 enterprise 
server and 8200 departmental SMP server, through the mid-range 
AlphaServer 2100 and 2000 SMP models, to the entry-level AlphaServer 
1000 and 400 servers.  Digitals AlphaServer 2100, 8400, and 8200 
systems all run the industrys fastest microprocessor, the Alpha 
21164 RISC chip.

Lotus Notes is the leading client-server platform for developing and 
deploying strategic groupware applications that help organizations 
communicate, collaborate, and coordinate strategic business 
processes within and beyond their organizational boundaries to 
achieve improved business results.  More than 7,000 companies and 3 
million people use Notes to improve key business processes such as 
customer service, sales and account management, and product 
development.  Lotus Notes supports all major operating systems 
including IBM OS/2, Warp, Apple Mac OS, Microsoft Windows and 
Windows NT, and UNIX platforms including IBM AIX, Sun Solaris, 
HP-UX, and SCO OpenServer.   Notes is also available as a NetWare 
loadable module for the Novell environment.

Lotus Development Corp., a wholly-owned subsidiary of IBM Corp., 
offers high quality software products and support services that 
reflect the company's unique understanding of the new ways in which 
individuals and businesses must work together to achieve success.  
Lotus innovative approach is evident in a new class of applications 
that allows information to be accessed and communicated in ways 
never before possible, both within and beyond organizational 
boundaries.  The company also provides numerous support services, 
both from its consulting division and its award-winning 24-hour 
support center.

Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client-server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digitals scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in todays global marketplace.
