                      DIGITAL NAMES ROD KELLER
               VICE PRESIDENT OF CONSUMER PC PRODUCTS
                          FOR THE AMERICAS


MAYNARD, Mass., November 8, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Rod Keller has been appointed vice president of 
consumer products for its Personal Computer Business Unit in the 
Americas.

     In the newly created post, Keller will lead Digital's existing 
retail PC sales and marketing efforts in the U.S. and drive planned 
expansion into Canada, Mexico, Central and South America, and the 
Caribbean. Before his promotion, Keller was U.S. director of 
consumer products for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit. 
Keller joined Digital in October 1994.

     Keller will continue reporting to Raymond L. Weadock, who is 
the Personal Computer Business Unit's vice president and general 
manager for the Americas.

     "Rod Keller's consumer PC experience is a valuable asset as we 
continue our push into retail," said Weadock. "Rod made a 
significant contribution to our progress in the U.S. during the past 
year. In that short time, we expanded distribution to more than 
1,700 retail outlets and attracted top-tier national chains. Now he 
will take on a broader role as we prepare to expand distribution 
over the next year."

     Digital's Starion PCs are available at regional and national 
retailers throughout the U.S., including AAFES (Army/Air Force 
Exchange Stores), Circuit City, CompUSA, Incredible Universe, 
OfficeMax, Sam's Club, Lechmere, and Nobody Beats The Wiz.

     "Just as we've made significant inroads in the U.S., Digital is 
positioned to become a powerful consumer PC brand throughout the 
Americas," said Keller. "We have an organization intensely focused 
on retail. And, with Digital's expertise in technology and service, 
we continue to create products that excite consumers."

     Keller brings more than 13 years of industry experience to his 
new responsibilities. Prior to joining Digital, Keller was sales 
director of consumer products at Compaq Computer Corporation. Before 
that, he was director and general manager of consumer products at 
Dell Computer Corporation. Keller holds a bachelor's degree in 
business administration from Southwest Texas State University.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
