              DIGITAL STORAGEWORKS SETS NEW PERFORMANCE
              STANDARD BY SUPER-CHARGING RAID ARRAY 410


        StorageWorks RAID Family 'Raises the Bar' in Meeting
     Customers' Storage Requirements in Multivendor Environments


MAYNARD, Mass., November 9, 1995 -- In a move that further 
distinguishes its StorageWorks products from competitors, Digital 
Equipment Corporation today announced a significant 67 percent 
performance boost to the StorageWorks RAID Array 410, making it the 
fastest and most reliable RAID subsystem available for multiplatform 
environments.  Now, high-end RAID users with even the heaviest I/O 
loads can access mission-critical business information faster than 
ever before.  

     "Digital's RAID Array family has consistently set the 
performance standard for high-end RAID storage solutions," said 
Penny Scharfman, StorageWorks marketing manager.  "By further 
enhancing the performance of the RAID Array 410, we are establishing 
a new benchmark to ensure customers' growing enterprise storage 
requirements are met.  Digital understands our customers' businesses 
depend on quick and reliable access to mission-critical information.  
Providing customers with that competitive advantage through the 
fastest and most advanced technology possible is our ongoing goal."

     Through enhanced Version 2.7 firmware, the RAID Array 410 
performance has been increased to 4,350 I/Os with a single 
controller configuration. This enables customers with heavy I/O loads 
to achieve higher throughput since more requests can be handled 
simultaneously; those customers with less demanding I/O operations 
benefit from an even shorter response time from their systems.  The 
new firmware, combined with the RAID Array 410's range of high-availability 
features, further positions the product as the superior RAID 
solution for meeting customers' evolving storage needs in 
multivendor environments.

     "The RAID Array 410 has enabled us to offer a real competitive 
advantage to our customers who require demonstrated performance," 
says Brian Casey, director of sales for Computer Peripheral 
Resources, a value-added reseller located in Natick, Mass.  "We're 
very enthusiastic about the newest enhancement because it ensures 
that Digital will maintain its position as the performance leader." 

StorageWorks RAID Array 410 -- Higher Performance RAID For 
Multivendor Environments

     Introduced in January 1995, the StorageWorks RAID Array 410 
provides reliable, expandable, cost-effective RAID storage for 
Hewlett Packard UX, IBM AIX, Sun Solaris and SunOS platforms.  
Expanding on their leadership position, the Storage Business Unit 
also plans RAID Array 410 support for Microsoft Windows NT in early 
1996.  This support will enable the growing base of NT users to 
benefit from high-performance RAID storage solutions for the 
enterprise.  

Availability and Pricing

     The RAID Array 410 performance upgrade will be available in 
January, 1996, and will be shipped directly to customers on a PCMCIA 
card for easy on-site upgrade.  

     The StorageWorks RAID Array 410 Subsystem is priced lower than 
any comparable RAID product for multivendor environments at $23,052 
for a 12.9 GB configuration, which consists of a StorageWorks 
six-channel SCSI controller with 32 MB read- and write-back cache, 
RAID software, and a StorageWorks office expansion enclosure with 
redundant fans and optimized power supplies. Dual-controller 
configurations of the RAID Array 410, which deliver increased 
performance and availability, start at $29,821.  The product is 
widely available through select distributors and value-added 
resellers (VARs).  For more information about Digital's complete 
line of StorageWorks products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967).

     The StorageWorks product line is a comprehensive family of 
disk, tape and optical storage subsystems, offering modular, 
competitively-priced, industry-standard solutions in customizable 
desktop, deskside, departmental and datacenter enclosures.  
StorageWorks products are available on multiple operating systems 
and hardware platforms, including Digital, Hewlett-Packard, IBM and 
Sun workstations and servers, and Novell and Windows NT 
environments.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha Platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
