                  Digital Brings "Whatever It Takes" Spirit 
         
                      and Technologies To Fall COMDEX '95
         
         
                 
LAS VEGAS, NEVADA -- Nov. 13, 1995 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation arrived at Fall COMDEX '95 ready to demonstrate 
it is the IT company customers can depend upon to deliver the 
most flexible and adaptable solutions for emerging 
connectivity needs.  
             
Visitors to Digital's exhibits will view demonstrations 
showing how Digital can help enterprise customers 
successfully deploy, interconnect and manage multi-tier 
client/server environments across the enterprise.
             
Systems Business Unit 
Booth #L4602 & 4802, North Hall, LVCC
             
Digital's Systems Business Unit is showcasing the 
complementary corporate technologies and competencies of the 
Digital/Microsoft "Alliance for Enterprise Computing" through 
a simulated toy car company.  eNTerprise Motors uses 
Digital's powerful family of Intel and Alpha systems, 
servers, and the fast, flexible, and affordable Digital 
Personal Workstations for all facets of its operations.
             
The price performance leading AlphaStation systems running 
Digital UNIX, along with the newly announced Digital Personal 
Workstation family running Windows NT, provide the hardware 
platforms for the product development area where applications 
such as Pro/ENGINEER from Parametric Technology Corporation, 
Microsoft's Softimage, and AVALON Applications from Avalon 
Software are used to create, manufacture and distribute 
product.   
             
Sales and Marketing is demonstrating QPS, a desktop 
publishing system from Quark; ARCView, a data mapping 
applications from ESRI; and FrontPage, a World Wide Web tool 
from Vermeer Technologies.  Digital's family of 64-bit 
AlphaServers provide the backbone of "eNTerprise Motors" 
Information Systems department.  The department also runs 
Microsoft SQL Server for Windows NT on a low-cost, scalable, 
high availability cluster technology that uses 
industry-standard components.  

Components Division 
Booth #L4002, North Hall, LVCC
             
The Multia and Printing Systems businesses will further 
distinguish themselves from their competitors by unveiling 
significant products at COMDEX.  To help deliver 
enterprise-wide application connectivity, Multia is 
announcing the new Pentium-based Multia MI enterprise client.  
The Multia MI enterprise client is the first product to 
provide high-speed connectivity, ease-of-use, and 
manageability in a highly integrated platform that bridges 
the gap between legacy applications and Windows NT.
             
In another unique introduction, the Printing Systems Business 
is answering the call of users seeking high-performance, 
premium-quality continuous tone color laser printers with the 
new Colorwriter LSR 2000 printer.  An affordable desktop 
color laser printer, the Colorwriter LSR 2000 printer 
provides the same near-photographic print output and 
processing power that previously was available only from 
expensive, production-quality printers.  
             
To demonstrate its position as the performance leader, 
Digital's Storage Business Unit will be showcasing the newly 
enhanced StorageWorks RAID Array 410, now the fastest and 
most reliable midrange RAID subsystem available for 
multiplatform environments. With the recently announced 67 
         percent performance boost, high-end RAID users with even the 
         heaviest I/O loads can access mission-critical business 
         information faster than ever before.
             
         Personal Computer Business Unit 
         Booth #L4402,  North Hall,  LVCC
             
         Attendees will be able to test drive new models from 
         Digital's entire showroom of personal computing vehicles for 
         the Information Highway, including the sporty new Celebris XL 
         personal workstations based on Intel's recently announced 
         Pentium Pro microprocessor. 
             
         Digital's personal workstation family of 
         processor-independent desktop computers -- including the 
         Celebris XL line -- enables simple migration to the latest 
         Intel Pentium, Pentium Pro and Digital Alpha processors, and 
         are the Windows NT platform of choice for technical users and 
         mission-critical computing applications.  The Prioris family 
         of award-winning PC servers provide mass transit 
         client-server computing for small workgroup applications to 
         large enterprise solutions.  The booth will also feature 
         advanced technology demonstrations of Digitals future Pentium 
         Pro and Pentium 133MHz symmetrical multiprocessing, 
         enterprise-class PC servers.
             
         Furthering its drive into the home PC market are the 
         company's recently announced Starion systems featuring 
         home-theatre-quality sound.  Digital's Starion retail PCs 
         feature powerful Intel Pentium processors, premium 
         JBL-powered sound, quad-speed CD-ROM drives, integrated 
         data/fax modems with telephone answering machine capability 
         and full-duplex speakerphone.  

         
         All models come pre-loaded with Windows 95 and a suite of 
         best-selling software titles.  For customers on the go, 
         Digital's line of highly acclaimed, Internet-ready HiNote 
         mobile computers will take them on the road in style.  
         Digital will display the recently announced quad-speed 
         version of its popular multimedia option for the HiNote Ultra 
         notebook computer -- this year's Laptop Innovation award 
         winner from PC Laptop Computers magazine.
              
         Digital Semiconductor 
         Booth #L4018,  North Hall,  LVCC
             
         Digital Semiconductor is demonstrating systems powered by its 
         Alpha RISC microprocessors, including the world's fastest 
         Alpha 21164-333MHz, as well as its new FX!32 software that 
         gives Alpha better-than-Pentium performance of 32-bit Windows 
         applications.  The booth features systems from 10 Alpha 
         partners running an array of popular imaging, animation, 
         computer-aided design (CAD), and mainstream Windows NT 
         applications.  Performance demonstrations of Digital 
         Semiconductor's merchant portfolio of PCI peripheral chips 
         for Ethernet networking, video/graphics, and PCI-to-PCI 
         bridging applications complete the exhibit.
             
         Internet Business Group 
         Booth #H423,  Las Vegas Hilton
             
         Digital's Internet Business Group will be demonstrating the 
         unique strengths that have made the corporation an Internet 
         leader.  The booth will include products such as the new 
         Digital Internet Tunnel and Workgroup Web Forum, a wide 
         choice of computing platforms, including Internet-ready 
         solutions built on Digital's award-winning Intel and 
         AlphaServers, and underlying networking architecture called 
         enVISN.  Also demonstrated will be a comprehensive set of 
         service and support options, and a variety of solutions from 
         a wide range of Internet partners.  Visitors to Digital's 
         Internet Village will be able to take a trip down the only 
         country road on the Information Highway, where they will be 
         able to log onto "A Very Vermont Store" and receive a free 
         gift in the mail representing the best of what Vermont has to 
         offer.
             
         Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
         client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
         worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Intel and 
         Alpha  platforms, storage, networking, software and services, 
         together with industry-focused solutions from business 
         partners, help organizations compete and win in today's 
         global marketplace. 
             
